{%- comment -%}
  Whether THIS request comes from a client that can show MCP Apps cards (docs/mcp-apps.md),
  so app-only tools exist for it. A modern request counts only its own declaration
  (helpers/protocol/negotiate ui_extension). A legacy request counts what its token's
  client declared at its last initialize (identity ui_apps, kept by commands/rpc/route). A
  request without a token never does.

  @param {object} proto    - the result of helpers/protocol/negotiate
  @param {object} identity - the caller resolved by dispatch, or nil without a bearer
  @return {boolean}
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  unless identity.authenticated == true
    return false
  endunless
  if proto.modern
    if proto.ui_extension == true
      return true
    endif
    return false
  endif
  if identity.ui_apps == true
    return true
  endif
  return false
%}
